# Compile-time reachability proof: provider-side eye-sync wiring uses MC 26.2 public API only.
# Date: 2026-11-01 (host, no device)
# Source: docs/analysis/bridge-sync-provider-reachability.java
# Env:   MC 26.2 client jar (Swift Craft Launcher meta/versions/26.2/26.2.jar)
#        LWJGL 3.4.1 shaded jar from the launcher payload
#        (vendor/amethyst-build/JavaApp/build/lwjgl-3.4.1.jar), JDK 25 (temurin-25).
#
# Why this matters: the provider has to (a) create an exportable timeline VkSemaphore on the game's
# VkDevice, (b) export its MTLSharedEvent via VK_EXT_metal_objects, and (c) append the timeline signal to
# the game's own frame submission (so it fires after the eye render passes). This probe proves javac
# resolves all three against the shipped MC 26.2/LWJGL APIs, i.e. no mixin or fork is required.
# The only private member involved is GpuDevice.backend (Vivecraft reads it through its access widener);
# the probe demonstrates the reflection fallback and the provider can alternatively ship its own
# access-widener entry.
#
# Command:
#   javac -cp "<26.2.jar>:<lwjgl-3.4.1.jar>" -d /tmp/vrmc-reach/out ProviderSyncReachability.java
#
